# Assignment 2 — Factory Method & Abstract Factory

**Theme:** Coffee Kiosk

## Part A — Factory Method
Creates one product (a `Drink`) — `Espresso`, `Latte`, or `Cappuccino` —
depending on which `DrinkCreator` subclass is used. The client never calls
`new Espresso()` directly.

## Part B — Abstract Factory
Creates a consistent family of order supplies — `Cup + Lid + Receipt` — that
must all come from the same brand. Two families: `ClassicSupplyFactory`
(paper cup, plastic lid, printed receipt) and `EcoSupplyFactory` (reusable
cup, biodegradable lid, digital receipt). `CoffeeKiosk` receives the factory
through its constructor and only depends on the `Cup`/`Lid`/`Receipt`
interfaces.

## Run
javac Main.java factorymethod/*.java abstractfactory/*.java -d out
java -cp out Main